From: RaikaShinohara <321751277+RaikaShinohara@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics_tcm_i2c - make the reset GPIO optional

The Samsung Galaxy S21 FE (SM-G990B2) does not wire a reset line to its
S3908; the controller is reset by cycling its supplies. GPIO 22, used
for reset on the OnePlus 9RT, is the panel reset on this board.
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm_i2c.c
@@ -892,7 +892,11 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to get supplies\n");
 
-	ts->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	/*
+	 * Optional: some boards (e.g. Samsung Galaxy S21 FE) do not wire a
+	 * reset line and rely on the supply power cycle instead.
+	 */
+	ts->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(ts->reset_gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(ts->reset_gpio),
 				     "failed to get reset GPIO\n");
